From: DeepSeek Harness <noreply@deepseek.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 07:05:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add long-press drag selection to the Android files screen

The Android files browser had no way to pick rows, so a long press had
nowhere to go and a drag only scrolled the list. Rows now carry a
transient selection: a long press starts a range at that row, dragging
extends it in display order (folders first, then files), and a second
long press while rows are selected keeps the current selection as its
base and adds another range instead of replacing it.

Tapping a row toggles it while anything is selected and opens it
otherwise, the path capsule shows the count and offers to clear the
selection, and the system back clears it before unwinding the folder stack. The
list watcher takes over the gesture on the Initial pass only once a row's
own long press has started the selection, so a press that turns into a
scroll before the timeout still scrolls and pull-to-refresh keeps
working. Selection keys are pruned when the listing changes and cleared
when the folder does.

